  <h2>What is Dhizuku?</h2>
  <p>
    Dhizuku is an open-source (GPL-3.0) tool created by iamr0s. Android
    reserves its most powerful management APIs for a single designated
    "Device Owner" app — the role enterprise fleet-management software
    normally fills. Dhizuku activates itself as the Device Owner, then shares
    those permissions with other apps through its API. No root is required.
  </p>

  <h2>What it gives you</h2>
  <p>
    Apps built on the Dhizuku API gain access to Android's own
    enterprise-grade controls — managing apps, users, and device policies as
    defined by the Device Owner APIs on your Android version. Dhizuku supports
    Android 6.0 through Android 17.
  </p>

  <h2>Before you activate</h2>
  <p>
    The official guide strongly recommends activating on a device set up
    <em>without any accounts</em> — if accounts are already configured, you may
    need to remove them first. On Android 12 and later, activating via
    <a href="/shizuku">Shizuku</a> can help avoid account-related errors
    (marked experimental by the developers). Knowing your exact Android
    version is step one — our free
    <a href="/scan">browser-based scan</a> reports it over USB.
  </p>
